WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.467
-We don't always have
enough time

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.634
to cover all of the recent news,
so here to recap

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.133
is one of our writers,
Amber Ruffin,

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.467
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:14.067
-You guys,
things have been crazy!

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:17.234
Okay, first of all,
the midterms were last week,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:20.400
and the whole nation
was like, what?!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.901
But then the red wave
didn't come,

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.400
and we were like, what?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.400
The whole thing was bananas.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.901
Okay, so,
Marjorie Taylor Greene won,

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.901
and I was like, what?

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.901
Then Stacey Abrams lost,
and I was like, what?

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.334
And then the race between
Raphael Warnock

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.667
and Herschel Walker
was too close to call,

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:41.501
and I was like, wha-a-a-a-a-at?

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.167
For the first time, I was like,

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.033
maybe there is voter fraud,

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.667
because there is no way someone
would want to give this man

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.000
an ounce of power.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.367
If you put this man
in charge of Georgia,

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.701
he's only gonna get it pregnant,

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:58.234
take it to another state,
and get it an abortion.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:00:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:00.367
Oh, no! [ Gasps ]

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:01.634
I'm too late!

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.634
Ohh!

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.300
That's at least six months,
right there.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.334
And then even though she's the
one who made him famous,

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.667
Oprah said to not vote
for Dr. Oz,

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:17.000
and I was like [laughing] what?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Girl, she created him,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.167
and then he lost his mind,
so she had to stop him.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.667
So, remember,
don't call him Winfrey.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.834
Call him Winfrey's monster.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.734
Then I found out that
25-year-old Maxwell Frost

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.033
got elected to Congress,

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.701
and I was like, "Go ahead,
Gen Z, what-what!"

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:37.033
And he was like, "No one says
what-what anymore."

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:40.033
And I was like,
"Okay, dang, children."

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.801
Then I heard the GOP is
turning away from Trump,

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.067
and I was like, what!

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.167
But then I found out that
they're turning towards

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:49.501
Ron DeSantis,
and I was like...what?

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.634
Ron DeSantis is the new face
of the GOP?

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:53.634
Let me get this straight.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.968
You went from this face

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:57.000
to this face?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.100
You're bad at faces.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.534
Then -- and this is real --

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.400
the United Nations
Climate Change Conference

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.067
ran out of food and water.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.901
[ Laughing ]
I was like, what?

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:10.167
You know damn well
that is too on the nose.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:12.334
That is like a Taco Bell
conference

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.000
running out of farts.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.667
So then I learned that someone
won $2 billion in the lottery,

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.000
and I was like, what?!

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.834
Man, if I won $2 billion,
I would be out of here.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.167
Between you and me,
it's terrible here.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:29.567
My boss is so needy.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:32.234
-Hey, that's not nice.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.734
-Not you!

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.567
Seth, you're one cool dude.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.234
-Aw, thank you.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.000
-[ Sighs ]

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.501
Then, the Astros won
the World Series,

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:44.667
and I was like, what?!

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.067
You mean to tell me

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:49.400
the dog from "The Jetsons"
won the World Series?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.901
And then I found out that
the Astros are a sports team.

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:54.734
Now, which sport --
that's none of my business.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:58.234
So, then I read that
a cruise ship docked in Sydney

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:02.300
had 800 people with COVID on it,
and I was like, what?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.634
Only 800?

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.133
A cruise ship without COVID

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:08.467
is like a Taco Bell
without farts.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:09.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:10.968
Guys, I'm just kidding.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.300
I love Taco Bell,
and I can prove it.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.501
[ Fart sound ]

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.000
So then...

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.167
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:25.334
-The script said
"tiny fart noise."

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.834
-But I had -- I had had
too much Taco Bell,

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:33.501
so it became
something different.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:37.167
So, then I read that
Elon Musk bought Twitter,

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.334
and I was like, "What?

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.667
This is gonna be bad!"

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.834
But then I read he was gonna
make people pay

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:44.000
for blue check marks,
and I was like, "What?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.567
This is gonna be hilarious."

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.901
And sure enough,
people bought blue checks,

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.234
and then they posed as famous
people and companies and stuff.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.234
It was great.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.868
I saw a fake Nintendo account

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.601
tweet Mario giving the finger,
and I was like, what?

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.968
Then I saw a fake
O.J. Simpson account saying,

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.934
"Not gonna lie,
I did that [bleep]"

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.667
[ Laughter ]
I was like, what?

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.667
But then there was
the best one of all.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.701
This is the funniest thing
I ever read.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.267
Someone started a fake
American Girl doll account

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.434
and posted the single best tweet
of all time.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.167
[ Laughing ] I saw that...

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:32.834
I saw that and I was like,

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.667
"That's what
I have been saying!"

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:38.100
Little white children get
these dolls and are like,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.434
"Will the carriage bring me
'round to the ball?

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.767
Will I make friends
at boarding school?"

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.100
And then a Black girl buys
this doll, and it's like,

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.601
"Will I get caught and taken
back to the plantation?"

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:49.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.334
When it comes to
American Girl dolls,

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.968
I have always been
and forever will be

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.300
like, what?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.767
Then I saw this clip
of Kamala Harris.

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:02.367
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.868
-And I was like, what?

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.868
What are you -- what?

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.534
And then I saw this clip.

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:11.367
-Who doesn't love
a yellow school bus, right?

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:15.033
Can you raise your hand if you
love a yellow school bus, right?

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:19.834
Just -- there's something
about the -- and most of us --

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:23.133
many of us went to school
on the yellow school bus, right?

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.467
-And I was like, what?

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.501
Do you need some -- like, what?

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.667
Like, why is -- what?

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.167
But then I saw this.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.267
-I love Venn diagrams.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:34.934
[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.934
I really do.
I love Venn diagrams.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:41.400
It's just something about those
three circles and the analysis

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.234
about where there is
the intersection, right?

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.567
Yeah, I see people, and you
agree with me, right?

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:49.400
-I was like, what?!

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.734
Why is no one
trying to save her?

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:55.534
But then I remembered
she said this.

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.868
-Under a Biden/Harris
administration,

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:00.767
we will decriminalize
the use of marijuana.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:03.934
-And I was like,
man, she's fine.

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:05.601
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

